\section*{Conditional L\({}^{2}\) Einstein gap for nonnegative curvature}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{A topological Einstein-energy gap}: A sufficiently small scale-invariant $L^2$ trace-free Ricci energy is claimed to restrict a simply connected closed nonnegatively curved four-manifold to the diffeomorphism types $S^4$, $\mathbb {CP}^2$, or $S^2\times S^2$. No extra geometric bounds are assumed.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Assume the companion classification: every closed connected smooth four-manifold with $\operatorname{Ric}=3g$ and sectional curvature $\ge0$ has universal cover isometric to round $S^4$, Fubini--Study $\mathbb{CP}^2$ normalized by $\operatorname{Ric}=3g$, or $S^2(1/\sqrt3)\times S^2(1/\sqrt3)$. Under that explicit premise, the claim gives an absolute $\epsilon_0>0$ such that any closed connected simply connected smooth four-manifold with $\sec_g\ge0$ and \[\int_M\left|\operatorname{Ric}_g-\tfrac14\operatorname{Scal}_g g\right|^2\,dV_g<\epsilon_0\] is diffeomorphic, without specified orientation, to $S^4$, $\mathbb{CP}^2$ or $S^2\times S^2$. The conclusion is topological rather than isometric, and the theorem is expressly conditional on the classification premise.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{A topological Einstein-energy gap}: A hypothetical countersequence is normalized and shown to satisfy initial geometry and Sobolev bounds. A uniform smoothing interval controls its high-curvature region and propagates the Einstein defect and negative-sectional-curvature error. The limit is a compact nonnegatively curved positive-Einstein space, whose companion classification identifies the topology and contradicts the sequence.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{A topological Einstein-energy gap}: Under exactly ass:classification (all closed Ric=3g nonnegative-sectional-curvature universal covers isometrically standard), the stated result gives the universal scale-invariant L\({}^{2}\) threshold and unoriented diffeomorphism conclusion. The original weaker premise was not established.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 348 describes Lean coverage for the strict-positive-curvature Einstein classification; zero-plane rigidity and the small-energy gap are separate.

\textit{A topological Einstein-energy gap}: No manuscript-specific Comparator is listed in the pinned inventory.

The documented selection does not cover the entire manuscript assertion relevant here.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

